+# Execution and proof scopes
+
+## New finite tests
+
+`check_restriction_control.py` passed **19 exact test methods** in normal Python
+and `python -O`. Their JSON result records are byte-for-byte identical.
+Deliberately false controls failed in both modes with nonzero exit codes.
+The checker contains no optimization-removable Python assertion statement.
+
+These are finite Gaussian polynomial quotient fixtures. They verify canonical
+weighted representatives, actual adjoints, source restriction, composition,
+theta-relation corrections, action commutators, full-jet minor formulas,
+occupation polynomials, raw confluent derivative factors, arithmetic unit and
+rectangular-inclusion maps, literal mass, and rational logarithm enclosures.
+They are not sampled zeta zeros and do not certify arithmetic integrals.
+
+The displayed calibration uses exact rational matrices. Its printed decimal
+logarithms and upper bounds come from rigorous rational atanh-series enclosures,
+with the precise remainder in NOTE (53). No floating-point eigenvalues are
+accepted as a gap certificate.
+
+## Inherited work
+
+All **31 manifest entries** in the delivered arithmetic-endpoint ZIP matched
+actual archive bytes and declared lengths. Its **18-method checker** passed
+fresh normal and optimized runs, with identical JSON result records. This
+replays finite tests only; it does not formalize the inherited analytic norm
+bound or reenact its Deligne archive reconstruction.
+
+## Reader
+
+Pandoc generated both MathML HTML and editable LaTeX without a math conversion
+warning. System Chromium rendered the self-contained HTML at 1440 x 1000 and
+390 x 844. Both contain 253 MathML expressions and no page-wide horizontal
+geometry overflow. Equation containers scroll internally on narrow screens.
+The desktop, mobile, and certificate-section screenshots were inspected.
+The browser's default packaged executable was absent and file-URL navigation
+was restricted; the final rendering used system Chromium and the generated
+HTML as in-memory page content. No remote resource is needed by the reader.
+
+## What is not claimed
+
+No new Lean run, no arithmetic moment/root interval certificate, no new
+uniform-in-tensor-degree upper bound, and no RH or GRH proof. The new general
+finite-dimensional identities have written proofs. The inherited analytic input
+is cited at its written source scope. No remote GitHub files or branches changed.
+
+An add-only integration patch is supplied for the collaboration. Its local
+application and byte comparison are recorded separately in
+`checks/integration-check.json`.
